{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1328071-trinity-core-weapon-cost-question","id":1328071,"title":"Trinity core weapon cost question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-29T06:14:58-07:00","id":1328071,"title":"Trinity core weapon cost question","content":"Just re-reading the weapon creation rules for creating some cool core tech weapon for aberrant and I found that for each dot of wealth you can add a tag to a weapon, so according to this rule an assault rifle would cost five dots, the same as a jet aircraft in the core book, so I looked at the gear section in the Aeon book and found that weapons cost fluctuate from one to tree dots even if they have many more tags, so what rules I follow? I missed something reading the weapon chapter in the core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T06:28:44-07:00","id":1328078,"title":"","content":"The cost of the weapon in Core is Tags -1. The exact wording I don't have now, but its more like, &quot;all weapons have one tag and another can be added for each dot in wealth&quot;, its described on weapon tags initial text, if not wrong.<br /> For Aeon the cost is different, it's tags - 4. Its written more like &quot;you can build a weapon with 4 + Wealth dots tags&quot;, but you got the idea. This info is rather on the cost description or in the tag description in Aeon, not sure.<br /> <br /> Just to add a few more related details that may past while reading (it happened to me a few times):<br /> Armors can have Wealth dots tags in Core and 5 + Wealth dots tags in Aeon.<br /> Vehicles can have Wealth dots tags (minimum equal to size) in Core and Wealth +1 (again minimum equal to size, minimum cost of 4 for Starships) in Aeon.<br /> <br /> For Aberrant specifically it is not written anywhere, as the technology chapter focus on Super-Science, but I would go for the same as Core, as the tech is showing up but its still not cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-29-2019, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T06:54:15-07:00","id":1328081,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification and quick reply, I still think that weapons in the core are still pricey, but your explanation make sense, I really hope that equipment in Aberrant will be expanded in a future technology sourcebook. Speaking of that iirc something about that and about cybernetic implants was mentioned is some podcast. I think an expanded view on the tech of the Aberrant era (and the social changes it will entails) would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","user":"Starkiller","date":". 07-29-2019, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T07:13:37-07:00","id":1328083,"title":"","content":"I was expecting more about regular tech in aberrant, at least some info about how the costs have changed with the new technology available. But I guess we will have to wait for a future supplement.<br /> <br /> For now we can build cybernetics using the rules for Super-Science, just pick Gifts or Edges that fit the idea of the Equipment and add the Networked flaw, possibly the Worn tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T09:02:51-07:00","id":1328106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1328071-trinity-core-weapon-cost-question?p=1328081#post1328081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the clarification and quick reply, I still think that weapons in the core are still pricey, but your explanation make sense, I really hope that equipment in Aberrant will be expanded in a future technology sourcebook. Speaking of that iirc something about that and about cybernetic implants was mentioned is some podcast. I think an expanded view on the tech of the Aberrant era (and the social changes it will entails) would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a supplement for Aeon coming out that, if I recall correctly, will have some expanded rules for hardtech implants as well as more Biotech. There is also a planned book (after Adventure! most likely) that takes place in between Aberrant and Aeon with lots of cybertech and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Also re:costs, you don't always have to personally bankroll your equipment. Paths can give you access to equipment you couldn't afford yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T10:43:19-07:00","id":1328122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1328071-trinity-core-weapon-cost-question?p=1328106#post1328106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is a supplement for Aeon coming out that, if I recall correctly, will have some expanded rules for hardtech implants as well as more Biotech. There is also a planned book (after Adventure! most likely) that takes place in between Aberrant and Aeon with lots of cybertech and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Also re:costs, you don't always have to personally bankroll your equipment. Paths can give you access to equipment you couldn't afford yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's this stuff<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>\u00c6on \u00c6xpansion: </b>A PDF supplement for the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> setting. The \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion will contain sections which will be added to this PDF supplement via Stretch Goals, as detailed below. The supplement currently contains sections on:<ul><li>VARGS (large battlesuits) and VARG rules</li> <li>Additional Aberrants and Aberrant Cults</li> <li>New Noetic Biotech</li> <li>New Cyberware and New Espionage-Related Hardtech</li> <li>Using psions in the modern day with the Trinity Continuum Core book</li> <li>New Weapons and Armor</li> <li>Nihonjin Superiors</li> <li>Essay on life and technology in 2123</li> <li>Psiads (characters with psi powers who are not artificially created, and tend to be less powerful but more flexible than traditional psions)</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}